Third-party provenance and notices
==================================

This repository is a workflow for integrating separately obtained source
trees. It does not distribute a complete Google kernel source tree, factory
image, KernelSU-Next source tree, or SuSFS source tree.

Google kernel source
--------------------

The workflow targets the Android 14 / Linux 6.1 GKI source obtained through
https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/manifest using the
common-android14-6.1 manifest branch. The device-matched common/ commit is
set in config/versions.env before a build. Google and Linux kernel copyright
and license notices remain applicable to that source tree and any resulting
derivative kernel image.

KernelSU-Next and SuSFS
-----------------------

build_ksu_next_susfs.sh obtains KernelSU-Next from
https://github.com/pershoot/KernelSU-Next , branch dev-susfs, and SuSFS from
https://gitlab.com/pershoot/susfs4ksu , branch gki-android14-6.1-dev. The
selected commits are recorded in the build proof and can be pinned in
config/versions.env after a reviewed successful build. Preserve their
upstream copyright notices and licenses when redistributing derived material.

Local integration logic
-----------------------

The repository's shell scripts and workflow configuration implement the
Pixel 7 Pro integration procedure. They are GPL-2.0-only unless a retained
upstream notice requires additional terms.
